-- CONTRACT --------------- errors/pure_violation_2.march

`mod LeakyPure` (declared `cap pure`) declares `needs IO.Random`, but a pure module cannot hold a capability: `needs` exists only to admit side effects, directly or through a stdlib wrapper such as `File.read` or `DateTime.now`. [pure_violation]

Remove the `needs` line, and move the code that needs it to a module without `cap pure`.

17 |   needs IO.Random
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^



-- CONTRACT --------------- errors/pure_violation_2.march

`gen` in `mod LeakyPure` (declared `cap pure`) calls `random_bytes`, which has side effects. [pure_violation]

Use pure functions (no IO, spawn, vault, clock, or random ops) in a `cap pure` module.

21 |     random_bytes(16)
